1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
You do not have one brain. You have two.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,000
Two cell populations build it. They never mix.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Otx2 cells build the forebrain and midbrain

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Gbx2 cells build the hindbrain

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Different chromatin states from the earliest embryonic stages

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,500
The same split shows up across species

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Two nervous systems evolved separately, then fused

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The paper says two lineages. "Two organs" is press framing.
